<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_armorkit_17.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Enhancement Shamans</span></h2>Crafted items are a quick way to gain power on a new character, but this shortcut usually means that you have to spend a sizeable amount of gold for these items early on, when they are the most powerful.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94272/dreadrunner-helm">
<img alt="Dreadrunner Helm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helm_mail_raidhunter_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dreadrunner Helm</span></a> is a high item level crafted Head piece, which is the best available option until you aquire your Tier pieces.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94271/dreadrunner-sabatons">
<img alt="Dreadrunner Sabatons" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boot_mail_raidhunter_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dreadrunner Sabatons</span></a> are a pair of very well stated Boots with 2 red sockets. Thanks to those attributes they nearly match their heroic raid counterparts in value and can be considered pre-BiS.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79328/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> provides the most Agility of any early available trinket options, making it the strongest of all pre-raid trinkets before having access to Celestial/<wbr/>Raid gear.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> is a very strong trinket option and incredibly easy to obtain if you are an Alchemist.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85830/raiment-of-blood-and-bone">
<img alt="Raiment of Blood and Bone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_mail_raidhunter_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Raiment of Blood and Bone</span></a> gives a quick item level boost, but will be replaced very fast.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85831/raven-lords-gloves">
<img alt="Raven Lord's Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_mail_raidhunter_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Raven Lord's Gloves</span></a> gives a quick item level boost, but will be replaced very fast.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_cat_trinket08.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Pre-Raid Enhancement Shaman Trinkets</span></h2>For trinkets, Enhancement Shamans aim for Agility, Mastery, Haste, or Critical Strike. Generally, two passive rppm trinkets are preferred if possible. Realm Procs per Minute (rppm) trinkets were added in Mists of Pandaria and have an average amount of procs per minute assigned to them. It is capable of proccing more then the stated amount, but should average out.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94511/vicious-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Vicious Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_speedoflight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vicious Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> is the highest item level trinket available once you have farmed the Shado-Pan Assault reputation to Friendly. Eventhough you will most likely overcap your Hit with this item it is still a major damage gain due to its extra stats from the item level.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79328/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> provides the most Agility of any available trinket options, making it the strongest of all pre-raid trinkets before having access to celestial gear.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> provides a lot of Mastery and a strong Agility proc, while being very easy to obtain. This makes it a very good choice for pre-raid gearing.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95665/bad-juju">
<img alt="Bad Juju" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_archaeology_troll_voodoodoll.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bad Juju</span></a> is providing a lot of Mastery and a strong Agility proc. The additional damage from the Voodoo Gnomes is most likely not impactful.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95625/renatakis-soul-charm">
<img alt="Renataki's Soul Charm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_bladestorm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Renataki's Soul Charm</span></a> is offering a lot of static Expertise, which can free up some secondary stats in reforges and the stacking Agility proc offers some unique snapshot opportunities for strong Flame Shocks.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Enhancement Shamans</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria, your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit or 2550 Hit Rating and 7.5% Expertise or 2550 Expertise Rating. Keep in mind that some abilities such as the  <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei Racial Heroic Presence will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your special (yellow damage) hits will no longer miss raid bosses, though your regular swings still might.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, raid bosses will no longer be able to dodge your attacks. They will, however, still be able to parry them. For the vast majority of raid bosses, you will be positioned behind them, and enemies cannot parry attacks from behind. Expertise will also add to your Spell Hit. By reaching 7.5% in both Expertise and Hit, you will be able to reach 15% Spell Hit.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Enhancement Shamans</span></h2>Try your best to match the sockets' gem color whenever possible. The main goal is to stack Agility with your gems, but the extra Hit or Expertise allows for more optimal gearing and reforging. Avoid gemming pure Hit or Expertise, except for Engineering gems. However, if your gear won't allow you to reach your caps, try to gem the rest of the way, trying to match socket colors.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Capacitive Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitive Primal Diamond</span></a>/<wbr/>
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76884/agile-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Agile Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Agile Primal Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c6">Red Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76692/delicate-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Delicate Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Delicate Primordial Ruby</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c11">Orange Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76670/adept-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Adept Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Adept Vermilion Onyx</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c9">Purple Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76680/glinting-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Glinting Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glinting Imperial Amethyst</span></a></div></li>
